parts.stem:
In a synthesis of tulobuterol, the first step involves the formation of chlorobenzene. Benzene reacts with $\text{Cl}_2$ in the presence of an $\text{AlCl}_3$ catalyst.

{{figure:pdf_visual_02.png}}

Fig. 5.2

The second step of the synthesis involves the reaction of chlorobenzene with $\text{ClCOCH}_2\text{Cl}$, also in the presence of an $\text{AlCl}_3$ catalyst, forming compound Q.

{{figure:pdf_visual_04.png}}

Fig. 5.4

parts.text:
Tulobuterol is produced from Q as shown in Fig. 5.5.

